=== A1.3 classes at orders 1..6 ===
order 1: 1 class, strong 1, self-converse 1
order 2: 1 classes, strong 0, self-converse 1
order 3: 2 classes, strong 1, self-converse 2
  order 3 (odd): self-converse classes with H = 3 mod 4: 1  e.g. [(2, 3)]
order 4: 4 classes, strong 1, self-converse 2
    rep     0  H=  1 |Aut|=1 strong=False self-converse=True  converse-rep=    0 scores=(0, 1, 2, 3) c3=0
    rep     2  H=  3 |Aut|=3 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=    5 scores=(1, 1, 1, 3) c3=1
    rep     5  H=  3 |Aut|=3 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=    2 scores=(0, 2, 2, 2) c3=1
    rep     4  H=  5 |Aut|=1 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=    4 scores=(1, 1, 2, 2) c3=2
  order 4 arc-usage profiles (nonzero usages; number of unused arcs):
    rep   0 H=1 profile [1, 1, 1] unused arcs 3
    rep   2 H=3 profile [2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1] unused arcs 0
    rep   5 H=3 profile [2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1] unused arcs 0
    rep   4 H=5 profile [4, 3, 3, 3, 1, 1] unused arcs 0
  labelled 4-tournaments by (self-converse, H): [((False, 3), 16), ((True, 1), 24), ((True, 5), 24)]
  order 4: self-converse iff H=1 mod 4 iff n>=0 iff c3 even: True
  order 4: self-converse classes with H != 1 mod 4: 0 ; non-self-converse classes with H = 1 mod 4: 0
order 5: 12 classes, strong 6, self-converse 8
    rep     0  H=  1 |Aut|=1 strong=False self-converse=True  converse-rep=    0 scores=(0, 1, 2, 3, 4) c3=0
    rep     2  H=  3 |Aut|=3 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=   11 scores=(1, 1, 1, 3, 4) c3=1
    rep     5  H=  3 |Aut|=3 strong=False self-converse=True  converse-rep=    5 scores=(0, 2, 2, 2, 4) c3=1
    rep    11  H=  3 |Aut|=3 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=    2 scores=(0, 1, 3, 3, 3) c3=1
    rep     4  H=  5 |Aut|=1 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=    9 scores=(1, 1, 2, 2, 4) c3=2
    rep     9  H=  5 |Aut|=1 strong=False self-converse=False converse-rep=    4 scores=(0, 2, 2, 3, 3) c3=2
    rep     8  H=  9 |Aut|=1 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=    8 scores=(1, 1, 2, 3, 3) c3=3
    rep    10  H=  9 |Aut|=1 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=   10 scores=(1, 1, 2, 3, 3) c3=3
    rep    12  H= 11 |Aut|=1 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=   12 scores=(1, 2, 2, 2, 3) c3=4
    rep    41  H= 13 |Aut|=1 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=   41 scores=(1, 2, 2, 2, 3) c3=4
    rep    40  H= 15 |Aut|=3 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=   40 scores=(1, 2, 2, 2, 3) c3=4
    rep    76  H= 15 |Aut|=5 strong=True  self-converse=True  converse-rep=   76 scores=(2, 2, 2, 2, 2) c3=5
